  "definition": "In this source, an ulcer refers specifically to peptic ulceration involving lesions in the mucosal lining. It is described as a disorder whose origins may lie in a long-term psychosocial-neuropathological process, with Helicobacter pylori framed as a possible secondary factor rather than the primary cause.",
